<title>UK: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>UNITED KINGDOM GOVERNMENT LIST (970317)</p>
<p>**************************************************************</p>
<p>* 1 May 97 - General election.					 *</p>
<p>**************************************************************</p>
<p>   Head of State..............Queen ELIZABETH 2</p>
<p>				- - - - - - - -</p>
<p>CONSERVATIVE PARTY GOVERNMENT</p>
<p>	  (Formed 11 April 92, Reshuffled 05 Jul 95)</p>
<p>Prime Minister.....John MAJOR</p>
<p>	  (also First Lord of the Treasury &amp; Minister for</p>
<p>	  the Civil Service)</p>
<p>First Secretary of State &amp;</p>
<p>	  Deputy Prime Minister.Michael HESELTINE</p>
<p>Lord Chancellor.....Lord MACKAY of Clashfern</p>
<p>	  (also Speaker of the House of Lords)</p>
<p>Lord Privy Seal &amp; Leader of the House of</p>
<p>	  Lords............The Viscount CRANBORNE</p>
<p>Lord President of the Council &amp; Leader of the</p>
<p>	  House of Commons..........Antony NEWTON</p>
<p>				- - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p>   Agriculture Minister............Douglas HOGG</p>
<p>   Chancellor of the Duchy of Lancaster..........Roger FREEMAN</p>
<p>   Chancellor of the Exchequer</p>
<p>	  (Finance Minister).......Kenneth CLARKE</p>
<p>   Chief Secretary to the Treasury..........William WALDEGRAVE</p>
<p>   Defence Secretary...........Michael PORTILLO</p>
<p>   Education &amp; Employment Secretary...........Gillian SHEPHARD</p>
<p>   Environment Secretary............John GUMMER</p>
<p>   Foreign &amp; Commonwealth Affairs Secretary....Malcolm RIFKIND</p>
<p>   Health Secretary.............Stephen DORRELL</p>
<p>   Home Secretary (Interior Minister)...........Michael HOWARD</p>
<p>   National Heritage Secretary..............Virginia BOTTOMLEY</p>
<p>   Northern Ireland Secretary.............. Sir Patrick MAYHEW</p>
<p>   Trade Secretary......Ian LANG</p>
<p>   Scottish Secretary...........Michael FORSYTH</p>
<p>   Social Security Secretary.......Peter LILLEY</p>
<p>   Transport Secretary ........Sir George YOUNG</p>
<p>   Welsh Secretary................William HAGUE</p>
<p>   Without Portfolio (Conservative Party</p>
<p>	 Chairman)................Brian MAWHINNEY</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>Speaker of the House of Commons</p>
<p>	  (lower house)...........Betty BOOTHROYD</p>
<p>Speaker of the House of Lords</p>
<p>	  (upper house).......See Lord Chancellor</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>   Bank of England (Central Bank) Governor........Eddie GEORGE</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>			   (End Government List)</p>
